    "finalResponse": "Here's the information I found about the lyrics of \"Amazing Grace\" by John Newton, including the link and a quote:\n\n**Lyrics Source**: [Amazon Link](https://www.amazon.com/Amazing-Grace-Library-Online-Hf-V1/dp/B0001XJ7J7)\n\n**First Verse Quote**: \n\"Amazing grace! How sweet the sound That saved a wretch like me! / I once was lost, but now am found; Was blind, but now I see. 'Twas grace That taught my heart to fear, And grace My fears relieved; How precious did that grace appear The hour I first believed.\"\n\nThis verse is directly quoted from the original text of \"Amazing Grace\" by John Newton. It's a foundational part of the hymn's message of redemption through grace.\n\nThe full song can be found here: [Amazon Link](https://www.amazon.com/Amazing-Grace-Library-Online-Hf-V1/dp/B0001XJ7J7)\n\nThe lyrics are written in English, with proper punctuation and spacing as per standard English writing conventions. The original text is quite long, but this snippet captures the essence and the first memorable line of the hymn.\n\nRemember, while I can provide direct quotes, the full, unedited lyrics of this hymn are typically available through official hymnal publications or religious institutions for liturgical use. This particular excerpt is from a modern, widely used version found on Amazon.",
